<title>SPAIN: Spain Dec industrial production rose 1.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain Dec industrial production rose 1.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Institute gave the following provisional figures (percentage change):</p>
<p> INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION		  DEC 96    NOV 96  DEC 95</p>
<p> Yr/yr					 1.8	 -1.9    -4.8</p>
<p> Avg yr to date vs yr ago	     -0.7	 -0.9     4.6</p>
<p>The INE gave the following breakdown (percentage change):</p>
<p>					     DEC 96   NOV  96 YR-TO-DATE</p>
<p> Energy				     -1.8	2.0     -0.5</p>
<p> Non-energy minerals, chemicals	2.8     -3.6     -2.0</p>
<p> Metals, precision tools		 2.4	0.8	2.3</p>
<p> Other manufacturing		     2.5     -4.8     -2.6</p>
<p> Consumer goods			    2.3     -5.6     -1.5</p>
<p> Capital goods			     3.0	1.6	3.0</p>
<p> Intermediary goods			0.9	0.2     -1.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Year-to-date column gives average increases.</p>
<p>The seasonally-adjusted December industrial production index fell 2.1 percent year-on-year versus a rise of 0.4 percent in November.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
